  "description": "<p>The University of Cumbria is one of the youngest universities in the UK. It was established in 2007 by merging St Martin&rsquo;s College, Cumbria Institute of the Arts, and University of Central Lancashire&rsquo;s Cumbria campuses. The university has already earned a good reputation for the excellent quality of education it provides for its students.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>The subject areas of the offered courses are diverse including, healthcare, business, education, sports, humanities, performing arts, law, criminology, forestry, and science.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>The University of Cumbria&rsquo;s acceptance rate is around 46% though this can vary slightly based on different courses and departments. The university now hosts and assists over 7500 students each year.</p>\n\n<p><strong>University of Cumbria</strong> <strong>rankings</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>#117 in university ranking, UK (The complete university guide 2021)</li>\n\t<li>#8 for quality of education (THE impact rankings 2020)</li>\n\t<li>#49 in accounting and finance (The Guardian 2018)</li>\n</ul>\n",
